What the NVIDIA License means for you
-------------------------------------
Both cuRobo and cuTAMP are under NVIDIA's source-available license, not an open-source
license. Two clauses matter here:

  §3.1 Redistribution — you may redistribute the Work only under this same license, with
       a complete copy of it included and all copyright/attribution notices retained.

  §3.3 Use Limitation — "The Work and any derivative works thereof only may be used or
       intended for use non-commercially", where non-commercial means research or
       evaluation purposes only.

So: **tandem as distributed is for research and evaluation use only**, because the planner
it vendors is. Installing it, running it, and publishing results from it are all fine. Using
it in a commercial product is not, without a separate license from NVIDIA.

If you need a distribution that is not subject to those terms, build tandem with the
vendored planner excluded and fetch it at install time instead:

    python tools/vendor.py --source <checkout>      # for local development only
    # then exclude src/tandem/_vendor/{curobo,cuTAMP} from the wheel

The exact pinned commits tandem vendors are recorded in
`src/tandem/_vendor/VENDOR.toml`, along with the paths trimmed from each tree and the
patches applied to it (`tools/patches/`).


Python dependencies
-------------------
tandem's runtime dependencies (typer, rich, pydantic, ruamel.yaml, numpy, platformdirs,
tomlkit, fastapi, uvicorn) and its optional extras (av, pyarrow, huggingface_hub,
rerun-sdk) are installed from PyPI under their own licenses and are not redistributed here.
